scussed C yet, but we can introduce. The instruction says we should still cover all candidates before final. So it's appropriate to bring C now.\n\nThus we will produce a public message: \"I see the arguments for A and B, but I think we should also consider Candidate C, who demonstrates rapid correct decision-making and stays calm in crisis, which are vital. While he has communication and egocentric concerns, these may be mitigated with training. Therefore I propose Candidate C as my provisional recommendation, and ask for thoughts on his crew cooperation and adaptability.\"\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: \"Building on the points raised about A's anticipation and B's reliability, I think C's decision quality and stress resilience are also critical.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"keeps calm in a crisis\", \"understands complicated technology\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\".\n\nWe need to state vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce output."}
